1
00:00:01,320 --> 00:00:04,300
Reading. Elias's story.

2
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,060
My name is Elias.

3
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:17,060
The time when I first met Nelson Mandela was a very difficult period of my life.

4
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:25,140
It was in 1952 and Mandela was the black lawyer to whom I went

5
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:25,980
for advice.

6
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:31,940
He offered guidance to poor black people on their legal problems.

7
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:36,080
He was generous with his time, for which I was grateful.

8
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:40,040
I needed his help because I had very little education.

9
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:52,480
I had to leave because my family could not continue to pay the school fees

10
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:53,660
and the bus fare.

11
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:57,580
I could not read or write well.

12
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:01,180
After trying hard, I got a job in a gold mine.

13
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:07,020
However, this was a time when one had got to have a passbook to live in Johannesburg.

14
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:11,480
Sadly I did not have it because I was not born there,

15
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:15,040
and I worried about whether I would become out of work.

16
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:19,680
The day when Nelson Mandela helped me was one of my happiest.

17
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:25,140
He told me how to get the correct papers so I could stay in Johannesburg.

18
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:28,620
I became more hopeful about my future.

19
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:32,580
I never forgot how kind Mandela was,

20
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:35,960
When he organized the ANC Youth League,

21
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:38,400
I joined it as soon as I could.

22
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:58,840
Black people could not vote or choose their leaders.

23
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,840
They could not get the jobs they wanted.

24
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:07,480
The parts of town in which they had to live were decided by white people.

25
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:14,080
The places outside the towns where they were sent to live were the poorest parts of South Africa.

26
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:16,640
No one could grow food there.

27
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:20,340
In fact as Nelson Mandela said: "...

28
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,040
we were put into a position in which we had either to accept we were less important,

29
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,740
or fight the government.

30
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:30,660
We chose to attack the laws.

31
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:52,380
but in 1963 I helped him blow up some government buildings.

32
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:58,400
It was very dangerous because if I was caught I could be put in prison.

33
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:05,300
But I was happy to help because I knew it would help us achieve our dream of making black

34
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:07,080
and white people equal.
